    "creation_reason": "Commit 4f92cc25 (the src-side PostgreSQL removal, MT-136/137/138 territory) deleted 26 test files. MT-141 inherited a tree with those tests already gone. A coverage sweep across BOTH src/ and tests/ found that of 57 deleted tests, 3 covered removed behaviour and 4 are covered elsewhere, but 47 cover production behaviour that is still live and either has no proof anywhere (33) or only partial proof (14). Deleting a test to reach a green compile is the exact failure MT-141 exists to prevent, so this coverage cannot be silently dropped. Under Operator decision 2026-09-10 (fast close), MT-141 closes on a complete disposition and this microtask carries the restoration as tracked, non-silent debt.",
    "why_a_separate_microtask": "Three reasons. (1) A predecessor microtask deleted them, not MT-141. (2) Seventeen items need an axum+reqwest HTTP harness and the whole set is 47 tests; folding that into MT-141 would hold MT-148 and the WP hostage. (3) Three items are blocked on a PRODUCT defect (no production store implements MemoryCapsuleIpcStore) and cannot be ported by any tests/-only microtask. Operator chose the fast path explicitly.",
    "operator_decision_2026_09_10": {
      "authority": "Operator reply: 'fast, close 141 with your exceptions implemented.'",
      "exceptions_implemented_in_mt_141": [
        "mt120_unauthenticated_caller_cannot_forge_the_reserved_native_principal",
        "mt120_invalid_session_token_is_401_and_never_downgrades_to_the_header_identity",
        "mt120_authenticated_save_stamps_derived_principal_without_rebinding_actor_id"
      ],
      "why_those_three": "They guard a live privilege-escalation check at src/api/knowledge_documents.rs:467 that had zero coverage at any layer. Restored into tests/knowledge_documents_api_tests.rs reusing its existing doc_server harness."
    },
    "urgency": "HIGH for the three security-relevant items and the Loom rollback variants; MEDIUM otherwise.",
    "operator_direction_2026_09_10": {
      "source": "WP-KERNEL-012-KB-READY-RECEIPT-WAIVER-20260910",
      "note": "Operator states repo governance will be abandoned soon and that only state recovery and status matter. Consequence for follow-ups: do not build the missing receipt emitter as governance work; MT-150 and the two routed product defects are state-recovery debt to carry into whatever replaces repo governance, not rituals to complete here."
    }
  },
